WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.490 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  in the depths of their underwater  Kingdom the mighty dragon Lords quaked  with fear before them prance Sun Wukong  The Monkey King  the legendary troublemaker had been  hatched from a stone schooled in divine  magic and was currently brandishing the  Dragonlords most treasured weapon this  magical staff originally large enough to  measure the depth of a great flood now  obeyed the monkey Kings will and shrank  at his touch terrified of this bill will  during power the Dragons graciously  allowed Sun Wukong to cap the staff The  Monkey King stowed the weapon away and  gleefully sped back to his kingdom to  show this treasure to his tribe of  warrior monkeys after a lavish  celebration Sun Wukong fell into a deep  sleep but just as he began to dream The  Monkey King quickly realized two things  the first was that this was no ordinary  slumber the second was that he wasn't  alone suddenly he found himself caught  in the clutches of two grizzly figures  at first The Monkey King didn't know who  his captors were but as they dragged him  towards their city's gates Sun Wukong  realized his deathly predicament  these were soul collectors tasked with  transporting mortals to the realm of the  Dead this was the domain of the death  Lords who mercilessly sorted souls and  designed gruesome punishments  [Music]  from here the kingdom of death was laid  out before him he could see the death  humans palaces and the fabled bridge  across the river and I her Manning the  bridge was an old woman who offered  worthy souls a bowl of soup after  drinking the spirits forgot their  previous life and was sent back to the  world of the living in a new form  further below were the souls not worthy  of reincarnation in this twisting maze  of chambers unfortunate spirits endured  endless rooms of punishment from  mountain spiked with sharp blades two  pools of blood and vats of boiling oil  but soon Wukong was not about to accept  torture or reincarnation as the soul  collectors attempted to drag him through  the gates The Monkey King whipped out  his staff and swung himself out of their  clutches his battle cries and the clang  of weapons echoed throughout the  underworld sensing a disturbance the ten  death lords swooped upon him but they  had never met such resistance from a  mortal soul what was this unusual  creature and was he immortal a god or  something else the Lord consulted the  book of death and life a tome which  showed the time of every living Souls  death not knowing what category this  strange being was under the death Road  struggled to find Sun Wukong at first  but The Monkey King knew just where to  look unfortunately the records confirmed  the death Lords claim soon Wukong was  scheduled to die this very night but The  Monkey King was not afraid this was far  from the first time he defied destiny in  his quest for wisdom and power his past  rebellions have earned him the power to  transfigure his body ride clouds at  dizzying speeds and govern his tribe  with magic and martial arts in this  crisis he saw yet another opportunity  with a flash of his nimble fingers The  Monkey King struck his own name from the  book before the death Lord could respond  he found the names of his monkey tribe  and swept them away as well  liberated from the bonds of death Sun  Wukong began to battle his way out of  the underworld he deftly defeated  endless swarms of angry spirits before  tripping on his way out of the kingdom  just before he hit the ground  Sun Wukong suddenly awoke in his bed at  first he thought the journey might have  been a dream but the Monkey King felt  his new immortality surging from the top  of his head to the tip of his tail with  a cry of triumph he woke his warriors to  share his latest adventure and commenced  another round of celebration  for more tales of death-defying  adventures in the underworld check out  these two myths choose carefully though  one of them does not end happily  [Music]

